  "System.Title": "Bug: sum() drops the first element, so sum([1,2,3]) returns 5 and mean() is wrong",
  "Microsoft.VSTS.Common.Priority": 2,
  "Microsoft.VSTS.Common.StateChangeDate": "2026-11-23T07:56:13.767Z",
  "System.Description": "<p><b>Repro:</b> in src/math.js, <code>sum([1,2,3])</code> returns 5 instead of 6. <code>mean([2,4])</code> returns 2 instead of 3. </p><p><b>Cause:</b> the loop in <code>sum(xs)</code> starts at <code>i = 1</code>, so <code>xs[0]</code> is never added. </p><p><b>Acceptance:</b> sum adds every element; an empty array still sums to 0; the existing tests in test/math.test.js pass. Keep the change to src/math.js. </p>",
  "System.Tags": "bug; wicked-proof"
 },
